{
 "_comment": [
  "Nominative Lithuanian place names, used to verify a birthplace",
  "recovered from 1996-1997 biography prose.",
  "",
  "Those pages print the birthplace in the locative ('Kaune', 'Klaipėdoje',",
  "'Šiaulių rajone') while the rest of the corpus stores the nominative.",
  "Suffix rules alone cannot do the conversion -- '-yje' yields both",
  "Panevėžys and Radviliškis -- so candidates generated by those rules are",
  "accepted only if they appear here. That lookup is what makes the",
  "conversion safe: a mis-parsed fragment produces no candidate in this",
  "list and is dropped rather than written.",
  "",
  "Derived from gimimo-vieta across the 39 non-archive elections, keeping",
  "values seen 3+ times: 1,357 of 21,951 distinct names, which resolves 454",
  "of the archive's 571 birthplaces against 465 for the full set. The tail",
  "is villages and parishes that no lookup would settle anyway.",
  "",
  "Regenerate with scripts/build_place_vocabulary.py."
 ],
